cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Wyss DBS Annotator: recording deep brain stimulation programming visits in an
  analysis-ready format
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lucia
    family-names: Poma
    email: lucia.poma@wysscenter.ch
    affiliation: Wyss Center for Bio and Neuroengineering, Geneva, Switzerland
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TODO: add before submission
  - given-names: Richard M.
    family-names: Köhler
    email: richard.kohler@wysscenter.ch
    affiliation: Wyss Center for Bio and Neuroengineering, Geneva, Switzerland
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TODO: add before submission
repository-code: https://github.com/neuromodulation/DBSAnnotator
url: https://dbs-annotator.readthedocs.io/
abstract: >-
  Wyss DBS Annotator records the programming visits that follow deep brain
  stimulation surgery, the appointments at which a neurologist or psychiatrist
  tests stimulation configurations and optimises them, over months or years as
  the parameters need adapting. It writes them to BIDS tab-separated files,
  capturing the relationship between the stimulation delivered at each
  configuration and the clinical response observed. It runs fully offline on
  iPadOS, Android, Windows, macOS and Linux, and produces PDF and Word reports for the patient
  record.
keywords:
  - deep brain stimulation
  - DBS programming
  - neuromodulation
  - clinical data capture
  - BIDS
  - Flutter
license: MIT
